# 白话层 v2 英文覆盖：对应 plain_zh_v2.ZH 的同一批 key，把重写后的中文翻成地道英文人话。
# 不译旧注释，译新 zh；忠实原义、不作占断。
EN = {
  "1-4": "You're at the top right now, right at the center of things with real power in your hands. This is when you can actually get something big done — but remember: the higher you climb, the more real substance you need to back it up. Don't coast on the title alone.",
  "2-4": "You're high up, but you hold your ground with gentleness — like wearing a yellow lower robe, nobility tucked inside. In a high position you don't put on airs or step out of bounds; you keep your luster within instead of flashing it around.",
  "9-4": "You're in charge, the one pulling people together, binding everyone with sincerity. What holds a group is trust that lasts — so rather than keeping the goodies to yourself, share them, and people will actually gather around you.",
  "10-4": "You're high up and you act decisively, charging straight ahead. But drive without restraint is dangerous even when you're right — the key to a decision is thinking it through carefully, not just being bold.",
  "10": "Lü is about keeping your footing and watching your step — like walking on a tiger's tail: stay alert, keep your manners, and you'll get through smoothly.",
  "11-4": "You're up high, yet you stoop to reach the people below. In a high place you can still humble yourself before the worthy — forgetting your rank to follow someone truly able. That's about as good as it gets.",
  "13-4": "You're in charge, and you're meant to click with someone below, but others are keeping you apart — at first it doesn't work. But what's right, even if briefly blocked, comes together in the end. Lead with sincerity and even a gap will open through.",
  "14-4": "You're up high, steady and upright, and people willingly follow you. Meet others with genuine feeling — without losing your temper, others still respect you. Authority grows from trust, not from punishment.",
  "15-4": "You're up high, modest and steady, and when someone still won't listen, you back it with firmness. Modest, yes — but you don't drop the boundaries. When virtue is more than enough and someone still won't fall in line, you have to show some teeth.",
  "16-4": "You're up high, steady, but propped up by a strong person below — you gain a helper yet can't be fully your own. Like a sick person kept alive by medicine — you're still standing only because someone's holding you up.",
  "18-4": "You're up high, steady, and you use a capable person to clean up the mess. Fixing things doesn't mean doing it all yourself — let the worthies handle it and take the credit: that's knowing how to use people.",
  "19": "Lin is about how to treat people from above — through what's right, not through raw power. The eighth month is the peak of fullness; it's there to warn you: the fuller you are, the more you should rein yourself in.",
  "19-4": "You're up high, steady, and you actually listen to those below — no know-it-all. A leader's wisdom is knowing people, not doing everything yourself. Put the right people in place and things get done without you killing yourself.",
  "20-0": "You're at the very bottom, farthest from the central figure, your view narrow — like a child watching the show. A shallow view is forgivable in an ordinary person; but if you want to accomplish anything, it won't do.",
  "21-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright — the case is easy to sort out. The matter is simple and the people involved are decent, so even a thorough look won't wrong anyone. Steady and fair people are fit to judge.",
  "22-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, connected to someone plain and simple below, and you find your way back to the unadorned. All the flash returns to the plain; all the decoration returns to the real. That plainness is Bi's true color.",
  "23-4": "You're beside the place of honor, leading a group in orderly fashion after the central figure, like a string of fish. Everyone follows what's right, each keeping their place without jostling — and the erosion stops.",
  "24-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, willing to draw close to someone below who's turned their life around — and you can settle and come back too. Being near good people lets you recenter. Gentle and low enough to listen, you find that peace.",
  "24-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, the only one among the crowd connected to the person below who's changed. Everyone else is lost; you alone turn back — following what's right, not the crowd. Walking your own road, your resolve is firm.",
  "24-4": "You're beside the place of honor, gentle and upright, able to return yourself — and you return deep and solid. Coming back to the root makes you unshakable — so there's no regret.",
  "24-5": "You're at the very top of Fu, but you're lost and won't turn back — farthest from the one who could save you. Lost and refusing to return means never looking back your whole life. This trouble isn't from outside; you brought it on yourself.",
  "26-4": "You're beside the place of honor, gentle, and you stop a surge of brute force — taking away its momentum, not yanking out its teeth. Checking strength isn't about meeting force with force; it's working on the root. Take away the root and the teeth aren't scary.",
  "27-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, at the peak of restlessness — the way you seek nourishment is completely off. Off-center and asking only from others, your path is already crooked. In time no one will help you — you've abandoned yourself.",
  "28-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, with strength but willing to be soft — you've pushed hard but not too far, so you can carry the load. Strength with give can bear responsibility — but with a burden on you, don't get distracted. One attachment and things go wrong.",
  "29-5": "You're at the very top of Kan, trapped by danger and unable to get out. At the extreme of danger with no way out, even time won't loosen it. Soft and not knowing how to change, you've trapped yourself.",
  "31-4": "You're in charge, upright, but you're feeling toward the wrong place — the connection is shallow. Like trying to move someone with your back turned, your heart can't reach them. But your intent is still right, so there's no regret.",
  "32-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong and measured, staying on the right path over the long haul. Strength with centrality gives endurance a root — keep to the middle and what you lost returns on its own.",
  "33-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strong but willing to soften — you can give up what you love and step away. Able to let go of attachments: that's the gentleman's withdrawal. The small man drowns in what he loves and can't leave.",
  "34-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong but not excessive — robust and upright. Strength with measure keeps it from violence. Strong without losing your bearings — so you can move ahead.",
  "34-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strong but willing to soften — robust, not reckless — and nothing blocks your way. Strength used the right way meets no obstacle. The point isn't how strong you are but whether you use it well.",
  "35-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, with gain and loss off your mind — you move without selfishness. When gain and loss don't drag at your heart, everywhere opens. The selfless person's advance reaches far.",
  "36-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, going into the dark, learning the truth inside, and leaving. Once you know the real situation, you can decide to go. See the sign and act that very day — don't put it off.",
  "38-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, meant to meet the person above but kept apart — you have to wind your way to connect. In a awkward split you can't go straight. Winding your way toward them is the art of adapting.",
  "38-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, reaching down to the strong helper below — the click comes easily. A gentle, centered you with a strong, able partner: joining up is quick and smooth. Going forward, nothing blocks you.",
  "40-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, resolving the world's difficulties by winning people's trust. You resolve trouble by winning hearts with sincerity — even the unfriendly come to believe. Where trust reaches, the difficulty dissolves.",
  "41-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, emptying yourself to take in whatever help comes. Step back and let people help, and helpers come on their own. An empty center doesn't push away what's offered.",
  "44-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center — nothing connects, so you can't settle. In Gou with nothing gained, your movement is unsteady. Too hard with no measure, you can't check the small troubles.",
  "46-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, with someone below who answers you — your rise comes step by step. Going up has a sequence, like climbing stairs one tread at a time. Gentle, centered, and using the worthy: you rise secure.",
  "47-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, with rigid forces before and behind — nowhere to stand. Stuck either way with nowhere inside to return: the road is spent. Soft and improper, you came to this.",
  "50-4": "You're in charge, gentle, receiving a strong, capable person below. A soft center taking in a strong helper makes the trust solid. Keep to what's right and you can bear the weight.",
  "52-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center — you've clamped down too hard. Stopping in the wrong place hurts you instead. A rigid, overdone person is never at ease inside.",
  "52-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, holding your tongue — your words have order. Curbing speech keeps it from rashness. Gentle, centered, and saying things in order, regret disappears.",
  "53-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center — leaving a settled place to rush ahead. Too rigid, you lose your grip and go without looking back. Only turning that force toward outside danger puts it to right use.",
  "53-4": "You're in charge, upright, reaching down to someone who matches you — but others keep you apart. A rightful connection, though blocked, can't be taken away. In time it opens on its own: that's the win of what's right.",
  "54-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — restless, reaching above yourself, and you end up lowered instead. Unsettled and grasping for more, you lose your footing. Soft and off-center, you can't get where you want.",
  "54-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strong but willing to soften, with no proper match — so you wait. Ability without an opening means waiting. No rash seeking, so though late, there's still a date.",
  "55-5": "You're at the very top of Feng — self-exalted, blinded, everyone's walked off. At the peak of fullness you hide yourself and people leave. High up with no contact with others, you end up alone.",
  "56-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center — you lose your resting place and your support. Too hard and people won't stay with you, so your place is gone. Even with right intent, danger can't be avoided.",
  "57-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong but over-yielding — yet your sincerity still gets through. Bowing under the bed is going too far, but centered and genuine, it reaches even the divine.",
  "58-0": "You're at the very bottom of Dui, upright, your joy harmonious but not loose. At the start of joy, with no attachments, the joy is simply harmonious. Harmonious without bias — that's right.",
  "58-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, only wanting others to please you. Chasing approval with no principles is a crooked path. Soft and improper, you came to this.",
  "58-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strong but willing to soften, holding firmly to what's right though not yet settled. Standing between wrong and right and keeping yourself — unsettled, yet with joy. Loathing the wrong is your integrity.",
  "58-4": "You're in charge, upright, but beside someone below who flatters you — and you're charmed into trusting them. Trusting what shouldn't be trusted, harm is on its way. High up and being charmed, you'd better stay watchful.",
  "61-4": "You're in charge, strong and sincere, binding the world together without selfishness. With faith you hold people together and all come to you. The real faith inside you is the root of trust itself.",
  "62-0": "You're at the very bottom of Xiaoguo — soft yet fond of rising, moving too fast. In an age of small excess, the low is right, not the high. Wanting to soar from the first step is why you rush.",
  "63-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, but temporarily without the means to act. Just keep to what's right — what you lost returns unasked. Don't chase; your way restores itself.",
  "63-4": "You're in charge, upright — your sacrifice is by faith, not by show. At Jiji's height, what counts isn't a grand rite but a full heart. When the heart is full, blessing truly lands on you.",
  "64-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — you can't cross alone but can lean on another. Soft and undecided, going solo sticks you. Attach to the strong and you can cross together.",
  "64-4": "You're in charge, gentle and upright, with someone below who answers you — crossing difficulty with soft-centered virtue. With virtue, your light shows itself. Empty within and appointing the strong, your faith reaches people.",

  "20-4": "You're up high, upright and near the center, and your own conduct is the example the world watches. Those above constantly examine their own gains and losses — that's the model others see. Get yourself right and people naturally follow.",
  "21-4": "You're in the judging seat, the one who decides, with both force and a gentle touch. Judging goes worst when it's all hard line — with dignity plus reading the moment, and a caution always in your heart, your rulings won't go wrong.",
  "25-3": "You're just above the lower center, with a streak of strength but willing to sit in a soft place — you can hold your part. Keep the edge sheathed, don't act rashly, guard what's yours to guard, and you won't err.",
  "25-4": "You're up high and upright, but this illness isn't something you brought on. An unlooked-for affliction like this heals on its own without fuss — force it with medicine and you'll only invite sickness.",
  "27-4": "You're up high and gentle, but you lean on the person above and can't sustain yourself. High yet unable to stand alone, relying on a worthy one is fine — for staying still, yes; for wading into danger, no.",
  "28-4": "You're up high, your force overdone, propped up by a little softness from above — but it won't last. An overly hard person can borrow softness for a brief flourish, yet that flower fades fast — spectacle without roots has nothing to brag about.",
  "29-4": "You're up high and upright but trapped in danger; the water hasn't filled yet, so holding steady gets you out. Before the danger brims over, level your heart, keep still, wait — and it recedes on its own.",
  "30-4": "You're up high, gentle, leaning on someone strong, your heart never quite at ease. Even at height, keeping a sense of danger is a good thing — with caution, you won't lose the clarity in your hands.",
  "32-4": "You're up high, gentle and steadfast, treating compliance as your right path. Yielding is right when it's toward people and following the good; but for deciding matters, you can't be soft all the way through.",
  "33-4": "You're up high and upright, matched with someone solid below — you retreat at exactly the right time. Step back when you should, without losing your center — that's the cleanest withdrawal: success achieved, then you step away.",
  "34-4": "You're up high and gentle, not treating brawn as achievement — so you actually let go of the brute force. At the peak of strength, reining yourself in is softness mastering force. Don't show off your might and there's no regret.",
  "36-4": "You're up high and gentle, right in the darkest hour — hiding your edge and keeping your heart intact. When the world's too dark, play dumb: that's Jizi's way. Light can't be put out — just hold on to it.",
  "37-4": "You're up high and upright, extending the way of the household to the whole world. When the head of a house sets it right, the world learns from them — no need to shout; things fall into place.",
  "38": "Kui is about divergence — two people, two camps, each with their own mind, drifting further apart. But the real point of this hexagram: find the same within the separate, find the connection within the different.",
  "39-4": "You're up high and upright yet stuck in danger — the one steering this whole predicament. A difficulty this big can't be carried by one. Draw friends and allies in with your steadiness, and the predicament breaks.",
  "42-4": "You're up high and upright, genuinely wanting those below to benefit — and that sincerity resonates. You wish them well from the heart and they answer in kind. Goodness that comes from the heart meets a great echo.",
  "43-4": "You're up high and upright — cut away what must be cut, and do it with measure. Removing the unworthy doesn't mean overdoing the force. Handle it through the middle way: no backlash, and the job gets done.",
  "44-4": "You're up high and upright, gathering the tiny sprout below into your fold — ability without display. When the time is right, the ones who should come will come to you on their own.",
  "44-5": "You're at the very top of Gou, rigid and high above, with no one to meet. Reaching the end and still finding no one means the road has narrowed — but rigid people don't act wildly, so even here you can avoid error.",
  "45-4": "You're up high and upright, the one holding people together — yet some still don't believe in you. Having position isn't the same as having trust. Build lasting virtue bit by bit; when hearts are won, that regret melts away.",
  "47-4": "You're up high and upright but squeezed by people above and below, unable to move. When others block you, go slowly instead of pushing — meet it with sincerity and the situation loosens by itself.",
  "48-4": "You're up high and upright, like the clear water in a well that nourishes people. Virtue with position lets your grace reach others. A centered, upright spring — everyone comes to draw from it.",
  "49-3": "You're just above the lower center, with strength but willing to soften, carrying the big task of change. If your heart is sincere you can scrap the old rules — strength and give working together, the job gets done and regret fades.",
  "49-4": "You're up high and upright, the one steering the change, the transformation out in the open. When a truly great person changes, the whole aspect shifts — no one needs to ask; people believe on their own. That's sincerity at its peak.",
  "50-5": "You're at the very top of Ding — strength in a soft place, virtue like jade. Hard yet warm, not to be violated. The way of the cauldron nourishing the worthy is complete here: use it any way and it goes well.",
  "51-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, when thunder strikes out of nowhere and you drop what you held. What's lost is a thing — don't chase it. Keep the steadiness inside; in time it returns.",
  "51-3": "You're just above the lower center, strength caught between two soft forces, unable to budge. Ability you can't use — you're simply boxed in. Wait for the moment that opens it up.",
  "51-4": "You're up high and gentle, amidst the thunder — danger coming and going, yet nothing lost. Hold the steadiness inside; danger is danger, but you won't break. Meeting trouble without losing your footing: that's the real skill.",
  "53-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, with a reliable superior watching over you — you advance on solid ground. Settled, you can nurture yourself at ease. Upright and supported, life goes smoothly.",
  "55-4": "You're up high, gentle and steadfast, able to gather the world's cleverness. Empty of yourself, you take in others' strengths — blessing and renown come on their own. That's Feng's most important art.",
  "56-3": "You're out making your way, with ability and money, but still not in the position you should have — that's why you're frustrated. Traveling, the first thing is somewhere to land. Ability without a place right now — don't rush; settle in first.",
  "57": "Xun is about seeping in like wind, silently — getting the word out and seeing the job through. Softness can penetrate, and having penetrated can still decide. That's Xun.",
  "57-0": "You're at the very bottom, just learning to work gently, your mind unsettled, wavering. Can't decide? Stop soft-pedaling — use some firmness when the moment calls for it. Soft with a spine of steel is what's right.",
  "57-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center, bowing again and again yet no one buys it. Yielding that isn't from the heart, just going through the motions, gets you slighted. Forcing it, you run out of road.",
  "57-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, caught between two forces. Yielding without losing yourself, you still gain something — that's the knack of getting along.",
  "57-4": "You're up high and upright, the one issuing orders, and your commands have measure. Strength with softness keeps them from being harsh. Say it clearly, then act — that's how a job gets finished.",
  "57-5": "You're at the very top of Xun, yielding too far, throwing away the backbone you should have kept. All giving way and you've no spine left — no spine, no way forward.",
  "58-5": "You're at the very top of Dui, the end of joy, dragging a crowd along for the fun. Charming people into good cheer, nobody can tell what you're really after. Joy at its peak that isn't rooted in what's right — the worst of Dui.",
  "60-4": "You're up high and upright, setting limits for yourself, and others gladly follow. Limits people don't find bitter are the good ones. Regulating yourself the right way, moving forward gets results.",
  "62-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strength but willing to soften — a little past the line but not too far, so you can still meet. Strength with give keeps you from excess. Ahead lies danger, so watch the timing and act by the moment.",
  "4-4": "You're up high, yet you ask for teaching with a child's open mind, gentle about it. Willing to listen and others are happy to tell you; high in station but not self-important — that's exactly why you can see clearly.",
  "12-4": "You're up high, steady and upright, able to turn a blocked situation around — but you keep a tight guard. When things are about to ease, be more careful than ever — keep the worst case in mind and your calm will hold.",
  "13-5": "You're at the very top, far from the like-minded one, with no one to join. Wanting unity and not reaching it means the time hasn't come. Since you can't join, there's nothing to regret.",
  "14-5": "You're at the very top — keeping faith, reading the current, strong yet in a soft place, following heaven without pushing. Faithful and compliant, honoring worthies to help you: this is someone heaven aids. And heaven aids those who first help themselves.",
  "16-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, the source everyone's ease depends on. Trusted like that, open your heart and don't suspect — doubt scatters them; sincerity keeps them close as a hairpin holds hair.",
  "17-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram — tied to a small player nearby, letting a big one go in the distance. Trading the big for the small: following people means choosing well; you can't have both.",
  "17-4": "You're up high, steady and upright, genuinely following the goodness of the world. You follow goodness itself, not any person — fix on the good and good people come of themselves.",
  "19-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong but measured, and the great one above answers you — your influence is right. Ability without bias makes the influence right; lead below with what's right and everywhere goes smoothly.",
  "64-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, strength and give together, crossing difficulty with that force and sustaining it. Before the task is done, what carries it through is strength plus endurance. Hold out and the work succeeds, the reward comes.",
  "53-5": "You're at the very top of Jian, rising above the fray, your bearing a model for others. Reaching the peak without clinging to position — what people learn is your demeanor; the aim is the far distance, not merely climbing.",
  "54-0": "You're at the very bottom, your standing not yet proper, doing your part from a lower place. Low but doing your duty well — unglamorous, yet workable. Settle where you are and do the task right.",
  "54-4": "You're up high, gentle and upright, with a capable person below answering you — virtue full yet humble. In high station you honor the worthy, valuing character over show. That fullness is like a moon nearing full — the weight is there.",
  "55-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, upright, but a dim person above hides your light — your ability can't get out. When the light's heavily covered, don't force your way out yet. Draw your edge in and you'll avoid error.",
  "55-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, in tune with a decent person below — even under cover you can act. Circumstances press you the same way, but with a like-minded ally the job gets done.",
  "56-0": "You're at the very bottom, just out in the world, lowly and narrow in view. Down and out, still nursing small grievances — trouble you bring on yourself. Soft and without bearing, you can't pull yourself up.",

  "56-4": "You're up high, gentle and upright, out on the road — you spend something but gain in the end. Culture within you means a small loss still ends in a good name. Gentle and steady, those above are willing to look after you.",
  "56-5": "You're at the very top of Lu — first gain, then loss, your very shelter burned. Traveling to the end and still arrogant: laughter first, wailing after. Throwing away the gentle way is your own doing.",
  "59-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, yet able to scatter your private self and turn toward the common good. Letting go of yourself and thinking of others — even off-center, no regret. Forget yourself and the scattered situation can be gathered.",
  "59-4": "You're up high and upright, pushing the word out and scattering even your own little circle. In a scatter, what matters most is the command. Issue it without selfishness and hearts can gather again.",
  "59-5": "You're at the very top of Huan — clearing out the harm and sending it far away. When the scattering ends, that's exactly when you can cut out the source of trouble. Keep what should be far far away and you won't err.",
  "60-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, unable to restrain yourself — then lamenting afterward. No check before, regret after: too late. But knowing what you're lamenting means there's still time to mend.",
  "60-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, someone above watching over you — at ease with your own limits. A limit that lets you rest isn't bitter. Gentle and upright, this measure holds.",
  "61-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, with no center inside. Without a center within, your joys and angers all hang on other people. Distrusting yourself, you can never settle.",
  "61-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, following the right path above, cutting off the private clique clean. Leaving private ties to follow what's right — that's a clean break. With the private cut, there's no aftermath.",
  "61-5": "You're at the very top of Fu — a loud name with nothing behind it. Sound without substance means trust is spent. Hollow and still not knowing to stop, the road is sure to dead-end.",
  "62-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center, unable to guard your own faults. Too hard and not watching your step, people take advantage. Self-guard is how you keep safe.",
  "62-4": "You're up high, gentle and upright, but can't do anything great — the benefit doesn't reach below. Position without the ability can't achieve the large. Small tasks are all you can manage; know your measure.",
  "62-5": "You're at the very top of Xiaoguo — wronging on and on without stopping, meeting no one. Excess to the end leaves you alone: that's exhaustion. Climbing high and never turning back, disaster is self-sought.",
  "63-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, upright, attacking from afar with force — long, then victory. After the task is done, undertaking things abroad is plainly hard. Use small men and you only stir more disorder.",
  "63-5": "You're at the very top of Jiji — your head already wet, danger arrived. At success's peak it's about to flip; trouble pours down from above. Failing to see the turn, you drown.",
  "29-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong and unbiased, right in the thick of danger. Don't reach for big gains now — a small one is enough. The big picture can't be held yet; keeping the small intact is the skill.",
  "39-0": "You're at the very bottom, just at the start of Jian — ahead is danger, back is solid ground. When the way is blocked, stop. Holding steady and keeping yourself, people end up praising your steadiness.",
  "40-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Xie — the difficulty just loosened; don't rush to act. Trouble barely gone and you stir again, you'll only invite more. Settle and breathe, and you'll avoid error.",
  "41-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram — three is too many, one is too few. Two together is the natural way. Three breeds suspicion, one wants a mate; trim the surplus and the pair forms.",
  "41-5": "You're at the very top of Sun — no need to keep cutting yourself and you can still help others. At the end of reducing, not reducing is the art complete. With that virtue you can go forward, win hearts, and not hoard the benefit.",
  "42-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Yi — those above give you resources, so you can take on something big. Backed from above, you can carry large things — but do them well to avoid blame.",
  "44-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, upright, able to check the sprout just starting below — the initiative is yours. While it's still in your control, no error. But the grip is tight and can't spread wide, so broad alliances aren't yet on the table.",
  "44-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, matched with the sprout below but losing your grip on it. Uncontrolled, people won't obey you. Having lost their hearts yet wanting to act, trouble springs up on its own.",
  "45-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — wanting to gather people and no one answers. Can't gather them, so you sigh. If you'd follow those above though, even reluctantly, it would pass muster.",
  "45-5": "You're at the very top of Cui — wanting people together and failing, anxious and afraid. Failing and fretting is caring too much. Knowing fear and not letting go, you still avoid error.",
  "47-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong and upright, but trapped by too much good living. The trouble isn't poverty, it's excess. The able person's honor comes on its own; meet it sincerely and you won't be dragged down.",
  "47-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, meant to connect with someone below but cut off by others — you can't reach them yet. Being separated only slows you; the bond remains. Keep calm and go on, and it ends well.",
  "47-5": "You're at the very top of Kun — tangled, unable to settle. At the end of difficulty you stir, and regret follows. But review what you've done and change it, and moving forward still gains.",
  "49-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Ge — the time isn't right to change, so hold steady. Change can't be forced. Before the time, keep the old ways; don't barge in with brute force.",
  "49-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid, wanting change — rash is danger, clear thinking works. Weighing a reform three times before deciding is utmost care. With a sincere heart, no one doubts you.",
  "49-5": "You're at the very top of Ge — everything that should change, inside and out, has changed. The transformation is complete; don't keep pushing. Just guard what you've achieved — beyond that is excess.",
  "50-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Ding — tip the legs to dump the old sediment. Clearing out old filth is worth it even if the posture looks bad. Turning the low into the noble, you won't err.",
  "50-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, upright with real substance — someone above answers you. A person of virtue, though envied, can't be reached. Keep to your own right path and it goes through.",
  "50-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and off-center — your movement is blocked. Too hard, you don't match those above, so the way is stopped. Turn back and find harmony, and in the end you gain.",
  "51-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Zhen — startled first, settled after; even fear needs measure. Fear first, calm after: that's knowing awe. With awe in your heart you avoid trouble, and even laughter keeps its bounds.",
  "51-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — panic costs you your footing, but moving can save you. Uneasy yet willing to act, no disaster. Fearful and able to change: you're teachable.",
  "51-5": "You're at the very top of Zhen — fear at its peak, your gaze unsteady. At this point you can't act. If you take warning before it reaches you, you're spared.",
  "52-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of stopping — reining in at the first stir. Stop before you move and stopping is easiest. Keep that restraint always and you won't err.",
  "52-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright — you've stopped, but those around you haven't. You're still, they're moving, and your heart isn't at rest. You've stopped yourself but haven't reached others.",
  "52-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, stopping at yourself, not reaching outward. Holding yourself from rash motion is your part. Self-restraint avoids error.",
  "53-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, advancing into an unsettled place. Unsettled, but you find support and can rest. Gentle and upright, you're spared.",
  "59-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Huan — like a strong horse coming to pull you out. At the start of scattering, rescue values speed. A strong force lends a hand and you cross.",
  "59-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong, picking your footing in the scatter and moving toward it. In a scatter, somewhere to lean brings ease. Strong and choosing well, regret disappears.",
  "60-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Jie — the time isn't right, so don't show yourself. Limitation means knowing the time. When the time's wrong, staying still is simply your part.",
  "60-5": "You're at the very top of Jie — binding yourself too tight, beyond what others can bear. A limit turned bitter won't last. Though the intent is right, the resolve is still worthy.",
  "61-0": "You're at the very bottom, the start of Zhongfu — your faith has no clear object yet. Faith fears divided hearts most. Let the mind wander and you're uneasy — so stay watchful.",
  "64-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, strong but knowing to brake yourself — no rash advance. Before the task is done, you can't hurry forward. Ability with self-restraint keeps you on the right road.",
  "64-5": "You're at the very top of Weiji — finally you can act and rejoice, but excess loses it. At the end, celebrating with your people is fine — just don't let joy run wild; overdoing it loses even what you held.",
  "17-5": "You're at the very top of Sui — following others to the end, the bond so firm it's like being tied. Hearts this united can't be bound by force; it's faith that binds. Sincere, and people stay on their own.",
  "19-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, all sweet talk to win people over. Pretty words with no substance get seen through eventually. Since you know it's wrong and worry, it's not too late to change.",

  "20-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, near the central figure — you can see the country's strength flourishing. Seeing things this good, you can step further in. With wide horizons, your advance won't be careless.",
  "21-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — biting a hard case and hurting yourself instead. Ability can't carry it yet you force it, so you pay a little. Luckily you don't bull straight on, so a bigger fault is avoided.",
  "27-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright, willing to ask the solid person below for teaching — and you ask with focus. In a high place, bowing to learn is itself compliance. Ask single-mindedly and you're nourished without error.",
  "30-5": "You're at the very top of Li — all your brightness and force spent outward. At clarity's peak you can judge. Punish the ringleader, leave the followers be — that's clarity used the right way.",
  "36-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, upright, right where light is suppressed — yet you can still do something. Removing a great harm can't be hasty. Force with discernment: that's the right way.",
  "38-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, alone with no one answering — but like-minded with a decent person below, trusting each other. Alone, an ally carries you through. Though precarious, you're not isolated.",
  "39-5": "You're at the very top of Jian — the further you go the harder, but coming back brings real gain. At difficulty's end it flips. Draw near that strong central figure and you can achieve — that's a rich return.",
  "43-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, too rigid and wearing it on your face — your resolve too obvious. Removing someone shouldn't be written on your face. Quietly do it, outwardly keep the peace, inner purpose unchanged.",
  "45-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, someone above watching over you — wait to be led before moving. Advancing needs a guide; don't shove ahead. With sincerity inside, even thin courtesy gets through.",
  "49-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright, someone above answering you — change only when the time comes. Change must wait for its hour. Gentle, steady, following above: doing it this way, no error.",
  "7-5": "The campaign is over; time to reward merit. Reward the merit, but don't hand over the power to govern too — the deserving can be given money and goods, not a fief and authority.",
  "2-2": "You're just above the lower center, not yet in your proper place, your talent still hidden. Having ability, don't rush to show off — just keep your part. Help others without claiming credit and you get a good result instead.",
  "4-2": "You're just above the lower center, off the right path — abandoning the one who should answer you to chase the one above. Seeing gain, you lose your principles and tear down your own foundation. Wrong person followed, going there is wasted.",
  "10-2": "You're just above the lower center, your view and conduct skewed, yet you push ahead anyway. Ability can't hold the task but you force it — you leap into danger yourself. Knowing your measure is how you stay safe.",
  "12-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — flattering to the extreme and bringing shame on yourself. Currying favor too long, even they despise you. The motive you hide ends up your disgrace.",
  "13-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, out of place — wanting to attack but unable, so you stop yourself. When the cause isn't just, the force won't come. Knowing you can't win and holding back is returning to what's right.",
  "16-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place, craning toward the one above to get your pleasure. Leaning on others for joy, you lose your principles and delay deciding — so regret keeps growing.",
  "24-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — lost and back, back and lost again. The back-and-forth is risky but won't sink you. This circling means your heart still isn't settled.",
  "25-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — standing where you shouldn't. Some trouble isn't of your making: that's the 'unlooked-for' calamity. But standing wrong, you meet it more easily.",
  "29-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — danger before and behind. With danger both ways, don't move. A rash step now only sinks you deeper.",
  "32-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, out of place — lingering where you shouldn't stay. Wrong place, however long, earns nothing. Endurance must be on the right path, not merely time served.",
  "35-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, out of place — near the center but unsettled. High position, virtue not keeping up: like a rat, greedy and timid. Carry on like this and the danger is plain.",
  "38-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — squeezed between two strong people. Unsettled and pressed, at first it's hard. Keep to what's right and wait, and it ends well.",
  "40-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — letting the wrong person hold the right place. Wrong station invites others to take it. Virtue not matching position brings trouble on yourself.",
  "42-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, out of place — applying the way of benefit in a time of hardship. Using what you received to relieve another's urgency: that's the right use. Done sincerely, people trust you.",
  "43-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, out of place — can't advance, can't decide. Unsettled and unable to step, you haven't seen clearly. If you can move along with the group, regret fades.",
  "46-2": "You're at the top of the lower trigram, upright — advancing like entering an empty town, no one in the way. Ability with right movement rises smoothly, like walking into an empty city, nothing blocked.",
  "46-5": "You're at the very top of Sheng — still climbing, but your mind's gone dim. Rising to the end and not knowing to stop is blindness. Only unceasing rightness can save you from this.",
  "50-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, out of place — a heavy burden beyond your ability. Wrong person for the role ruins the work. Thin virtue, high station: you pull yourself down.",
  "52-5": "You're at the very top of Gen — still generously holding that restraint, not letting up. Ending with such solid restraint is the way fulfilled. Unchanging over time, you reach a good close.",
  "55-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright — a dim person above hides your light. When the light's covered, don't rush to show yourself. Build up sincerity then emerge, and the cover opens by itself.",
  "56-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright — settled out in the world, with means and a helper. A place to land outside, resources within and help without. Gentle and steady, you settle yourself.",
  "59-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright — breaking the private clique to make one whole. Scattering private factions is the greatest achievement: uniting everyone into one is beyond the ordinary.",
  "62-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram, gentle and upright — a little past the line, but not offending above. Exceed what should be exceeded, don't reach where you shouldn't. Knowing to hold back, you avoid trouble.",
  "63-3": "You're just below the upper trigram, gentle and upright — even after success, always on guard. Complete yet ever prepared, you don't fail. Planning in quiet times: that's the wise person.",
  "58-1": "You're at the center of the lower trigram — a streak of strength but genuine with people, joy from the heart. Sincere joy, no one suspects you're faking. Keep that sincerity and regret disappears.",
  "54-5": "You're at the very top of Guimei — the rites complete but no true feeling inside. Form without substance, and the task can't be completed. All name, no reality — nothing to recommend it.",
  "56": "Lu is about being away from home, not on your own turf. In that spot, keeping low and easy actually gets you further — this isn't a bad hexagram; it reminds you not to push too hard under someone else's roof, but to settle in first.",
}
